From: raidenkl <1740512636@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: rk817: re-apply the playback path after power up

"Playback Path" is only applied when its value changes, but the DAPM
power-up sequence rewrites the output stage with the defaults from
playback_power_up_list (class-D off, DACD down).  As a result only the
very first PCM stream after selecting a path is audible; every later
stream stays silent until userspace toggles the control away and back.

Re-apply the currently selected path at the end of the playback
power-up, passing it as pre_path so the helper does not recurse into
the power-up it just finished.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rk817_codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rk817_codec.c
@@ -456,6 +456,9 @@
 #define RK817_CODEC_CAPTURE_POWER_DOWN_LIST_LEN \
 	ARRAY_SIZE(capture_power_down_list)
 
+static int rk817_playback_path_config(struct snd_soc_component *component,
+				      long pre_path, long target_path);
+
 static int rk817_codec_power_up(struct snd_soc_component *component, int type)
 {
 	struct rk817_codec_priv *rk817 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
@@ -488,6 +491,18 @@
 			snd_soc_component_write(component, RK817_CODEC_APLL_CFG4, 0xa5);
 		}
 		rk817_restart_dac_digital_clk(component);
+
+		/*
+		 * The power-up list above restores the output-stage defaults
+		 * (class-D off, DACD down).  "Playback Path" is only applied
+		 * when its value changes, so without this the output stays
+		 * muted for every PCM stream opened after the first one.
+		 * Passing playback_path as pre_path skips the recursive
+		 * power-up inside rk817_playback_path_config().
+		 */
+		if (rk817->playback_path != OFF)
+			rk817_playback_path_config(component, rk817->playback_path,
+						   rk817->playback_path);
 	}
 
 	if (type & RK817_CODEC_CAPTURE) {
